o 0, `s->ndst == 0`, so `cp_decode(s, s->dst, 0)` takes the `tree[lo-1]` path at `lib.c:200` and returns `s->lit[287]`'s symbol field, which can be up to 287 — far past the 32 entries of `cp_dist_extra_bits`/`cp_dist_base`. Instrumented trace on the reproducer: `ndst=0 nlit=288 lensym=257 len=3 dsym=32`.\n- **Measured values at index 32:**\n\n  | | `cp_dist_extra_bits[32]` | `cp_dist_base[32]` |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | C, gcc -O0 (= the reference build; `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` sets no `-O`) | 1 | **0** |\n  | C, gcc -O2/-O3/-Os | 3 | **0** |\n  | Rust | 8 | **3** |\n\n  So `backwards_distance` is **0** in every C build (both bounds checks pass, `switch(0)` → default self-copy, decoding continues) but **3** in Rust (`out - 3 < begin` → immediate error).\n- **Distinguishing inputs** (`_audit/oob2/OOB2_zeros8`, 714-byte raw deflate; `_audit/oobpng/OOB2_wrapped.png`, 777-byte PNG):\n  - `cp_inflate(stream, 714, out, 4096)`: **C** → 604 non-zero bytes written, returns 0, `cp_error_reason = \"Attempted to overwrite out buffer while outputting a symbol.\"`; **Rust** → 0 bytes written, `cp_error_reason = \"Attempted to write before out buffer (invalid backwards distance).\"`\n  - `load_png_mem(png, 777)`: **C -O0 → SIGSEGV**; **C -O2 → glibc `double free or corruption (out)` abort**; **Rust → returns `{w=8, h=8, pix=NULL}`, `\"DEFLATE algorithm failed\"`.**\n  - PNG head: `89504e470d0a1a0a0000000d49484452000000080000000808020000004b6d29dc000002d049444154789cfde005081000000000f9ff7f93ffffffff…`\n- **Note:** this divergence is masked if the consumer itself declares the tables `extern` in a non-PIE binary (copy relocations flatten both to the executable's layout) — it manifests for any normal consumer or `dlopen`.\n- **Fix:** pack all six tables into one `#[repr(C)]` static reproducing the reference build's order/alignment and export the individual symbols as aliases into it.\n- Latent second instance (not reachable, for the record): `cp_len_extra_bits[31]` = `0` in C (alignment pad) vs `16` in Rust (`cp_permutation_order[0]`). Unreachable because lit/len symbols from any written tree slot are ≤ 287, so `symbol-257 ≤ 30`.\n\n### 2. `cp_dynamic` case 16: C reads `lens[-1]`, Rust substitutes `0` (MEDIUM)\n\n- **C `lib.c:215, 221`:** `uint8_t lens[288 + 32];` is **uninitialized**; `case 16:` does `lens[n] = lens[n - 1];`, and at `n == 0` this reads the byte immediately below the array on the stack (in practice `lenlens[18]`).\n- **Rust `lib.rs:423-424`:** `let prev = if n > 0 { lens[(n - 1) as usize] } else { 0 };`\n- **Distinguishing input** (`_audit/lm1/LM1_v18_7`, 60 bytes, hex `05e0830b` + 56 zero bytes): a dynamic block with `lenlens[16]=1, lenlens[0]=2, lenlens[18]=7` whose first code-length symbol is 16. Built with **gcc -Os** the C reads `lens[-1] == 7` and writes 4096 bytes of `0x80`; Rust writes 0 bytes. (gcc -O0/-O1/-O2/-O3 happen to have `0` in that slot and therefore agree with Rust.)\n- This is formally indeterminate in C, but it is a *distinct behavioral substitution* and is **not** one of the three paddings listed as accepted, so it belongs here rather than in the accepted section.\n\n## FUNCTIONS VERIFIED FAITHFUL (one line each)\n\n| C function | C lines | Rust lines | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `cp_make_pixel_a` | 9-16 | 60-62 | Faithful. |\n| `cp_make_pixel` | 17-24 | 65-67 | Faithful (`a = 0xFF`). |\n| `cp_would_overflow` | 76-78 | 182-184 | Faithful (assert-only). |\n| `cp_ptr` | 79-82 | 187-193 | Faithful: `uint32_t*` scaling and truncating `count/8`. |\n| `cp_peak_bits` | 83-98 | 196-214 | Faithful, incl. `count += bits_left` on the final-word branch and x86 shift masking. |\n| `cp_consume_bits` | 99-106 | 217-227 | Faithful, incl. u64→u32 truncation of the masked value. |\n| `cp_read_bits` | 107-116 | 230-240 | Faithful (asserts elided). |\n| `cp_rev16` | 117-123 | 243-250 | Faithful. |\n| `cp_build` | 124-154 | 259-317 | Faithful: `codes[len]++`/`first[len]++` order, `slot` zero-extended, `(code << (32-len)) \\| 