se-2's duplicated body, case-3's `int` sum then `/2`, and the `y++, prev = raw, raw += len` increment order. |\n| `cp_convert` | 464-484 | 800-833 | Faithful: `src++` per row, `src += bpp` in the for-increment (after the body), `*dst++` per case, no-op default. |\n| `cp_get_alpha_for_indexed_image` | 485-493 | 836-846 | Faithful (`(uint32_t)index >= trns_len`). |\n| `cp_depalette` | 494-508 | 849-877 | Faithful (`plte[c*3+k]`, `++x, ++src`). |\n| `cp_get_chunk_byte_length` | 509-511 | 880-882 | Faithful. |\n| `cp_out_size` | 512-514 | 885-887 | Faithful, incl. left-to-right `((w+1)*h)*bpp` wrap order. |\n| `load_png_mem` | 515-758 | 891-1081 | Faithful: all 20 checks in the same order, `cp_make32(ihdr)+1` truncated to `int`, the **unsigned** `(int64_t)w*h*sizeof < INT_MAX` comparison, `malloc(datalen)` with sign-extended negative `datalen`, `datalen/offset += len` unsigned wrap, `data+offset` sign-extended, `out = pix + size(4) - size(bpp)`, and the `free(data); free(img.pix); img.pix = 0` error tail. |\n\n**Other checks:**\n- **Tables (item 5):** mechanically extracted and compared. `cp_fixed_table` is exactly 320 bytes, run-lengths `[(8,144),(9,112),(7,24),(8,8),(5,32)]` — identical to `cp_make_fixed_table()`. `cp_permutation_order` (19), `cp_len_extra_bits` (31), `cp_len_base` (31), `cp_dist_extra_bits` (32), `cp_dist_base` (32) are all element-for-element identical.\n- **Error strings (item 1):** all **26** assignments extracted in source order and compared byte-for-byte — **26/26 identical**, including the two-literal concatenation in `cp_stored` (single space: `\"…within stored (uncompressed) stream.\"`), the concatenation in `cp_block`, the typo `\"innapropriate window size detected\"`, and the duplicated `\"invalid image size found\"`.\n- **Struct layout (item 6):** `cp_state_t` 2464 bytes / align 8, all 18 field offsets match C (`bits 0, count 8, words 16, word_count 24, word_index 28, bits_left 32, final_word_available 36, final_word 40, out 48, out_end 56, begin 64, lookup 72, lit 1096, dst 2248, len 2376, nlit 2452, ndst 2456, nlen 2460`). `cp_image_t` 16/`0,4,8`, `cp_pixel_t` 4/`0,1,2,3`, `cp_raw_png_t` 16/`0,8` all match.\n- **ABI:** exported symbol set and types identical (`cp_error_reason` in `.bss`; six tables in `.data`; `cp_inflate`, `load_png_mem` in `.text`).\n\n## KNOWN / ACCEPTED DEVIATIONS (as stipulated)\n\n1. `assert()` treated as a no-op. Confirmed necessary: building the C **without** `-DNDEBUG` aborts on `cp_consume_bits:100` and `cp_decode:202` for inputs the Rust handles. All differential testing used `-DNDEBUG`.\n2. `codes`/`first`/`counts` padded 16→256 in `cp_build` (`lib.rs:266-268`); `lenlens` 19→256 (`lib.rs:393`); `lens` 320→576 (`lib.rs:413`). I quantified the blast radius: on my independent corpus, **85** cases differ between the *unpadded* C and Rust, and an instrumented build proves **every one** is attributable — 82 to `lens` overrunning index 319 (e.g. `fuzz/png/m00916_ok_ct2_f5_7x5_l6.png`, where `n` reaches 427 and the C stack-smashes into SIGSEGV while Rust returns `\"DEFLATE algorithm failed\"`), 3 to the `lens[-1]` read of divergence #2. Zero cases with no flag.\n\n## THEORETICAL-ONLY (not distinguishable in practice; listed for completeness)\n\n- `in_bytes * 8` (`lib.c:304`) and `(s[0] << 24)` (`lib.c:375`) are signed-overflow UB in C; Rust computes them with wrapping/u32. Identical on x86-64 gcc for all inputs.\n- `pix_bytes = w * h * sizeof(...)` (`lib.c:608`) narrows to 32 bits *before* the ×4; Rust (`lib.rs:973-975`) computes in i64 then truncates. Equal mod 2³² for all inputs, and the preceding guard makes the value in-range regardless.\n- `while (length--)` (`lib.c:289`) vs `while length != 0 { …; length -= 1 }` (`lib.rs:511-516`): identical iteration counts for every `int`, including negatives, under release (wrapping) arithmetic. A debug build with overflow checks on would panic where C wraps — the crate sets `panic = \"abort\"` but relies on release defaults for overflow checks.\n\n## VERIFICATION METHODOLOGY\n\nBuilt the C reference (`gcc -DNDEBUG` at `-O0/-O1/-O2/-O3/-Os`) and the Rust `cdylib`, plus a C **oracle** carrying *exactly* the three accepted paddings. Determinism was forced with ASLR off, an `LD_PRELOAD` zeroing `malloc`, and 128 KB deterministic-pattern pads around every input/output buffer (without these, out-of-bounds reads of the input make **both** sides ASLR-dependent and produce ~1300 lines of spurious diff). Both sides confirmed self-deterministic.\n\n- Author's corpora: 895 PNGs + 25 deflate streams + 2500 mutated PNGs → **0 diff lines** vs the padded oracle.\n- My independent corpora: 1481 structured PNGs (chunk-length wrap-around, w/h wrap, all colour-type × bit-depth × filter × interlace grids, palette/tRNS length grids, byte-exact truncation sweeps) + 3449 deflate streams (stored LEN/NLEN grids × bit-misalignments, zlib levels 0-9, degenerate/empty Huffman trees, 3300 random streams), each run across 4 input alignments × 7 `out_bytes` including `-1` (~137k `cp_inflate` calls) → **0 diff lines** vs the padded oracle.\n- Edge harness: `png_length` swept ±12 and at `{-1,-2,-8,-9,-1000,INT_MIN,INT_MAX}`, 7 unaligned input pointers, `cp_inflate` with negative/extreme `in_bytes`/`out_bytes`, and 8 runtime mutations of the public tables (including out-of-range lengths > 15 and permutation entries > 18) → **0 diff lines**.\n\nDivergences #1 and #2 were found by hand-constructing bitstreams to reach `cp_decode`'s `tree[-1]` path and `cp_dynamic`'s `n == 0` path; neither is reachable by undirected mutation of valid PNGs, which is why the author's fuzz corpus missed them."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1389,"cache_read_input_tokens":205270,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1389,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Mzv